From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 10:56:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Accept the non-x86_64 SoC-aware schedule count in
 test_soc_aware

test_soc_aware hardcodes 142 schedules for the first graph, a value
only x86_64 produces. hopcroft-karp drives its DFS by iterating an
FxHashSet (std HashMap), whose iteration order depends on hashbrown's
SIMD group width: 16 with SSE2 on x86_64, 8 on aarch64 (NEON) and on
the generic backend (riscv64). The heuristic then picks a different
maximum matching and ends with 141 schedules on the first graph, every
one within max_delta_soc. Reproduced with the same source, Cargo.lock
and rustc 1.99.1 under qemu-user for riscv64gc and aarch64 (both 141;
x86_64 142, independent of RAYON_NUM_THREADS); upstream's own cargo
tests, including validate_sum_of_node_weights, pass on riscv64.
Upstream's Python tests only run on x86_64, so its released aarch64
wheels fail this assertion too. Branch the expected value on the
machine instead of skipping the test.

Upstream-Status: To upstream [not submitted from this automated port run]
---
 test/test_eflips_schedule_rust.py | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/test/test_eflips_schedule_rust.py b/test/test_eflips_schedule_rust.py
index 5aed547..3fb702a 100644
--- a/test/test_eflips_schedule_rust.py
+++ b/test/test_eflips_schedule_rust.py
@@ -1,5 +1,6 @@
 import json
 import os.path
+import platform
 import unittest
 from eflips_schedule_rust import solve
 import networkx as nx
@@ -57,7 +58,11 @@ class TheTestCase(unittest.TestCase):
             number_of_schedules.append(nx.number_connected_components(G))
 
         # Print the number of connected components
-        self.assertEqual(number_of_schedules, [142, 64, 21, 11, 9, 5, 5, 2, 1, 1, 1, 1])
+        # hopcroft-karp walks an FxHashSet, whose iteration order follows
+        # hashbrown's SIMD group width (16 on x86_64, 8 on aarch64/riscv64),
+        # so the heuristic finds an equally valid plan one schedule shorter.
+        first = 142 if platform.machine() in ("x86_64", "AMD64") else 141
+        self.assertEqual(number_of_schedules, [first, 64, 21, 11, 9, 5, 5, 2, 1, 1, 1, 1])
 
 
 if __name__ == "__main__":
